From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:45:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iio: light: tsl2583: Add apple,als-calibration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The live ADT of the iPads carries the unit's resolved LSCI ambient-light
calibration in the light sensor's alsCalibration property: on the iPad 6
an LSCI v2 record, the 8-byte header (version 2, one record at offset 8,
72 bytes in all) and one 0x40-byte record. Only the IPSW's ADT has the
unresolved syscfg/LSCI placeholder.

Let the bootloader copy those bytes into apple,als-calibration, as it
does for the touchscreen calibration. Systems whose boot firmware
provides a SysCfg NVMEM cell keep using nvmem-cells.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux a782d501 (J71t ledger 9.1); his
 firmware-name property for a private LSCI file becomes a property the
 bootloader fills from the ADT, so no unit data is packaged.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/iio/light/tsl2583.yaml           | 29 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/tsl2583.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/tsl2583.yaml
index 988c634b5..ca799972e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/tsl2583.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/tsl2583.yaml
@@ -11,9 +11,10 @@ maintainers:
 
 description: |
   Ambient light sensing with an i2c interface. The Apple CT819 and CT821
-  factory calibration is stored in SysCfg. On systems where the SysCfg NVMEM
-  provider is created by boot firmware, the static board tree omits the
-  NVMEM link and firmware adds both NVMEM properties before kernel handoff.
+  factory calibration is stored in SysCfg. Boot firmware either copies the
+  resolved record into apple,als-calibration or, where it creates the SysCfg
+  NVMEM provider, adds both NVMEM properties before kernel handoff. The
+  static board tree carries neither.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -37,6 +38,15 @@ properties:
   vcc-supply:
     description: Regulator that provides power to the sensor
 
+  apple,als-calibration:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8-array
+    minItems: 8
+    maxItems: 1024
+    description:
+      Apple factory LSCI ambient-light calibration record, the raw bytes of
+      the ADT alsCalibration property as resolved by iBoot. Used instead of
+      nvmem-cells when present.
+
   nvmem-cells:
     description:
       Apple factory LSCI ambient-light calibration data. Boot firmware must
@@ -68,6 +78,7 @@ allOf:
           - nvmem-cells
     else:
       properties:
+        apple,als-calibration: false
         nvmem-cells: false
         nvmem-cell-names: false
 
@@ -86,4 +97,16 @@ examples:
             nvmem-cell-names = "calibration";
         };
     };
+  - |
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        light-sensor@39 {
+            compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
+            reg = <0x39>;
+            /* Copied by the bootloader from the ADT; header only here */
+            apple,als-calibration = [00 02 01 08 48 00 a2 f8];
+        };
+    };
 ...
